1
00:04:42,857 --> 00:04:48,857
Set sail for Muppet mayhem!

2
00:09:25,714 --> 00:09:31,714
Muppet Treasure Island is a family, comedy,
adventure film directed by Brian Henson.

3
00:14:08,571 --> 00:14:14,571
After telling the story of Flint's last journey to young Jim Hawkins, Billy Bones has a
heart attack and dies just as Jim and his friends are attacked by pirates.

4
00:18:51,428 --> 00:18:57,428
The gang escapes into the town where they hire out a boat and crew to find the
hidden treasure, which was revealed by Bones before he died.

5
00:23:34,285 --> 00:23:40,285
On their voyage across the seas, they soon find out that
not everyone on board can be trusted.

6
00:28:17,142 --> 00:28:23,142
Long John Silver, played by Tim Curry.

7
00:32:59,999 --> 00:33:05,999
Billy Bones, played by Billy Connolly.

8
00:37:42,857 --> 00:37:48,857
Mrs. Bluveridge, played by Jennifer Saunders.

9
00:42:25,714 --> 00:42:31,714
Jim Hawkins, played by Kevin Bishop.

10
00:47:08,571 --> 00:47:14,571
The Great Gonzo / Dr. Bunsen Honeydew / Waldorf / Mudwell the
Mudbunny / Zoot (voice), played by Dave Goelz.

11
00:51:51,428 --> 00:51:57,428
Kermit the Frog / Rizzo the Rat / Beaker (voice), played by Steve Whitmire.

12
00:56:34,285 --> 00:56:40,285
Muppet Treasure Island is a 1996 American musical swashbuckler comedy film directed
by Brian Henson and the fifth theatrical film featuring the Muppets.

13
01:01:17,142 --> 01:01:23,142
Adapted from the 1883 novel Treasure Island by Robert Louis Stevenson, similarly to its predecessor The Muppet
Christmas Carol (1992), the key roles were played by live-action actors, with the Muppets in supporting roles.

14
01:05:59,999 --> 01:06:05,999
The film stars Muppet performers Dave Goelz, Steve Whitmire, Jerry Nelson, Kevin Clash, Bill Barretta, and Frank Oz in various
roles, as well as Tim Curry as Long John Silver and introducing Kevin Bishop in his film debut as Jim Hawkins.

15
01:10:42,857 --> 01:10:48,857
The film was released in the United States on February 16,
1996, by Buena Vista Pictures Distribution.

16
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
It grossed $47 million worldwide.

17
01:20:08,571 --> 01:20:14,571
It also received generally positive reviews from critics.

18
01:24:51,428 --> 01:24:57,428
It is the second Muppets film to be produced by Walt Disney Pictures,
whose parent company would later acquire the Muppets in 2004.

19
01:29:34,285 --> 01:29:40,285
The film explores themes of island, pirate gang,
puppet, treasure hunt, puppetry.

20
01:34:17,142 --> 01:34:23,142
The tone is lighthearted.
